WEBVTT

00:07:29.038 --> 00:07:30.991
doesn't mean that I won't be successful.

00:07:31.015 --> 00:07:32.761
It doesn't mean anything other than,

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:35.465
I just don't know how to answer
that particular question,

00:07:35.489 --> 00:07:37.872
which can be a loaded thing
in and of itself.

00:07:38.813 --> 00:07:41.138
AG: Those kinds of questions
can stump candidates

00:07:41.162 --> 00:07:42.797
and make interviewers feel clever.

00:07:42.821 --> 00:07:44.559
I once interviewed for a writing gig

00:07:44.583 --> 00:07:46.226
where the manager opened by asking

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.757
what my favorite pair of shoes was.

00:07:48.781 --> 00:07:51.245
Objection, your honor, relevance?

00:07:52.006 --> 00:07:55.365
Interviewers also love to ask
open-ended questions.

00:07:55.389 --> 00:07:57.107
Lauren Rivera: In the United States,

00:07:57.131 --> 00:07:58.809
we love open-ended job interviews

00:07:58.833 --> 00:08:00.750
where people ask you about your hobbies,